    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0187",
      "sequence": 199,
      "meaning": "A heavenly voice tells sages, siddhas and gods not to fear: for their sake the Lord will assume human guise and descend with his portions in the noble solar dynasty. Kaśyapa and Aditi had performed great austerity and received this boon earlier; they have appeared as King Daśaratha and Kauśalyā in Ayodhyā. The Lord will enter their home as the four brothers who crown Raghu’s lineage, fulfil all of Nārada’s words, and descend with the supreme Power. He will relieve Earth of every burden, so the gods may be fearless. Hearing the divine assurance, they return comforted; Brahmā reassures Earth and then goes to his realm, instructing the gods to assume monkey bodies and serve Hari’s feet on earth.",
