      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0188",
      "sequence": 200,
      "meaning": "The gods return to their homes and Earth’s heart finds rest. Gladly obeying Brahmā without delay, they assume forest-creature bodies on earth, possessing immeasurable strength and splendour. Armed with mountains, trees, nails and teeth, the wise heroes watch for Hari’s path and fill mountain and forest with their splendid hosts. Śiva says he has told these lovely events and now resumes what he had set aside: in Ayodhyā ruled Daśaratha, renowned in the Vedas as the jewel of Raghu’s line, pillar of dharma, treasury of virtues, wise and inwardly devoted to the bow-bearing Lord. Kauśalyā and his other beloved queens were pure in conduct, devoted to their husband and firmly humble at Hari’s lotus feet.",
