    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0189",
      "sequence": 201,
      "meaning": "One day King Daśaratha grieves inwardly that he has no son. He immediately visits his teacher, clasps his feet and explains all his joy and sorrow. Vasiṣṭha comforts him in many ways and promises four sons famed through the three worlds who will remove devotees’ fear. He summons sage Śṛṅgī and performs the auspicious sacrifice for obtaining sons. As the sage offers with devotion, Fire appears holding the sacrificial sweet and declares that everything Vasiṣṭha intended has succeeded. The king must divide the oblation among the queens in fitting portions. Fire vanishes after instructing the assembly, while Daśaratha is submerged in supreme joy beyond what his heart can contain.",
