    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0190",
      "sequence": 202,
      "meaning": "Daśaratha immediately summons his beloved queens. He gives half the sacrificial food to Kauśalyā, divides the remaining half into two, gives one portion to Kaikeyī, then divides what remains again and, with Kauśalyā’s and Kaikeyī’s hands, joyfully gives both shares to Sumitrā. Thus all the women conceive and their hearts fill with immense happiness. From the day Hari enters their wombs, joy and prosperity spread through all worlds; every queen in the palace becomes a treasury of beauty, virtue and radiance. After a happy interval, the hour of the Lord’s manifestation arrives: conjunction, ascendant, planets, weekday and lunar date all turn favourable, and all moving and unmoving creation rejoices at Rāma’s birth, the root of bliss.",
